---
title: European robin
---
# European robin

The European robin is a small, round, orange-breasted chat of European woodland
and gardens, unrelated to the American robin despite the shared name. Both sexes
hold winter territories and sing through the dark months to defend them, which
is unusual among European songbirds. It follows digging animals, and in Britain
gardeners, to take invertebrates turned up from the soil. The orange breast is a
signal in territorial disputes, which are frequent and occasionally fatal. See
[[turdidae]].
